IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`
IMPORT `ss-general`
IMPORT `ss-rates`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — GOAL 2: ENTITLEMENT.
--
--   "Is the person entitled to jobseeker support, sole parent support or the
--    supported living payment on this day?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_32.txt — ss 20-24, 26,
-- 29-30, 32-36, 40.

§ `Goal 2 — entitlement`

§§ `Jobseeker support (ss 20-26)`

-- s 21 "(1) A person (P) has a work gap if— (a) P is not in full-time
-- employment; or (b) P is in employment but is losing earnings through a
-- health condition or injury". s 23 "An applicant for jobseeker support meets
-- the age requirement if the applicant is— (a) at least 18 years old, in the
-- case of an applicant without a dependent child: (b) at least 20 years old,
-- in any other case." s 24 "(1) ... P has no or minimum income if P has— (a)
-- no income; or (b) income of less than the amount that would reduce the
-- applicable rate of jobseeker support to zero. (2) If, during a temporary
-- period, P has enough income to reduce the applicable rate ... to zero, ...
-- P's entitlement ... is not affected". s 20 "A person is entitled to
-- jobseeker support if the person— (a) has a work gap; and (b) is available
-- for work; and (c) meets the age requirement; and (d) meets the residential
-- requirement; and (e) has no or minimum income." s 26 "A person (P) is not
-- entitled to ... jobseeker support if— (a) P is a full-time student ...; or
-- (b) P is unemployed because of ... a strike; or (c) ... took leave ... for
-- the purpose of undertaking employment-related training."
@ref ss 20-24, 26
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant, j IS A `Jobseeker facts`, r IS A `Rate facts`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to jobseeker support` a j r d IF
        ((NOT j's `in full-time employment`) OR j's `losing earnings through a health condition or injury`)
    AND j's `available for work under s 22`
    AND `the age of someone born` (a's `date of birth`) `on` d AT LEAST (IF a's `has a dependent child` THEN 20 ELSE 18)
    AND `meets the residential requirement` a
    AND (   `the weekly rate of` `jobseeker support` `, rate facts` r GREATER THAN 0
         OR j's `income high only for a temporary period`)
    AND NOT j's `a full-time student`
    AND NOT j's `unemployed because of a strike`
    AND NOT j's `left work for employment-related training`

§§ `Sole parent support (ss 29-33)`

-- s 30 "A person (P) meets the sole parent requirement if P is the mother or
-- father of, and caring for, at least 1 dependent child aged under 14 years
-- and— (a) P is single; or (b) P's spouse or partner has died; or (c) P's
-- marriage or civil union has been dissolved; or (d) P is living apart from,
-- and has lost the support of or is being inadequately maintained by, P's
-- spouse or partner; or (e) P has lost the regular support of P's spouse or
-- partner because [of a sentence]". s 29 "A person is entitled to sole
-- parent support if the person— (a) meets the sole parent requirement; and
-- (b) either— (i) is not in a situation of split care ...; or (ii) is in a
-- situation of split care and is the 1 parent who is entitled ...; and (c)
-- meets the residential requirement; and (d) is aged 20 years or over." s 33:
-- on the day the youngest dependent child turns 14, sole parent support
-- expires.
@ref ss 29, 30, 32, 33(2)
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant, s IS A `Sole parent facts`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to sole parent support` a s d IF
        s's `the mother or father of, and caring for, a dependent child under 14`
    AND (CONSIDER s's `youngest dependent child born on`
         WHEN JUST born THEN d LESS THAN `add years` born 14
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
    AND NOT a's `relationship situation` EQUALS `with a supporting spouse or partner`
    AND NOT s's `in split care and not the entitled parent`
    AND `meets the residential requirement` a
    AND `the age of someone born` (a's `date of birth`) `on` d AT LEAST 20

§§ `Supported living payment (ss 34-36, 40)`

-- s 35 "(1) A person (P) has restricted work capacity if P is permanently
-- and severely restricted in P's capacity for work because of a health
-- condition, or because of injury or disability arising (in either case)
-- from an accident or existing from birth. ... (3) P is severely restricted
-- ... if MSD is satisfied that P is incapable of regularly working at least
-- 15 hours a week in open employment." s 34 "A person is entitled to the
-- supported living payment if the person— (a) has restricted work capacity
-- or is totally blind; and (b) meets the residential requirement; and (c) is
-- aged 16 years or over." s 36: not if "self-inflicted and brought about by P
-- with a view to qualifying for a benefit".
@ref ss 34-36
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant, l IS A `Supported living facts`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` a l d IF
        (   (    l's `restriction permanent`
             AND l's `hours a week able to work regularly in open employment` LESS THAN 15
             AND l's `restriction from a health condition, or an accident, or from birth`)
         OR l's `totally blind`)
    AND `meets the residential requirement` a
    AND `the age of someone born` (a's `date of birth`) `on` d AT LEAST 16
    AND NOT l's `restriction or blindness self-inflicted to qualify`

-- s 40 "(1) A person (C) is entitled to the supported living payment if— (a)
-- MSD is satisfied that C is required to give full-time care and attention at
-- home to a person (P) who would otherwise have to receive institutional care
-- (and who is not C's spouse or partner); and (b) C meets the residential
-- requirement; and (c) C is aged— (i) at least 18 years, in the case of an
-- applicant without a dependent child; or (ii) at least 20 years, in any
-- other case."
@ref s 40(1)
GIVEN a IS AN Applicant, l IS A `Supported living facts`, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` a l d IF
        l's `required to give full-time care at home to someone who would otherwise need institutional care`
    AND NOT l's `the person cared for is the carer's spouse or partner`
    AND `meets the residential requirement` a
    AND `the age of someone born` (a's `date of birth`) `on` d AT LEAST (IF a's `has a dependent child` THEN 20 ELSE 18)

§§ `The entitlement goal`

@ref ss 18-24, 26, 29-30, 32-36, 40
@export Whether a person is entitled to a main benefit on a day under the Social Security Act 2018 (NZ), and not barred by ss 18-19 (another main benefit, superannuation or a veteran's pension; unlawful presence or a temporary visa): jobseeker support (work gap, available for work, 18 or 20 by dependants, residence, income below the cut-out, not a full-time student, striker or trainee); sole parent support (a parent caring for a child under 14 without a supporting partner, not the other parent in split care, residence, 20 or over); the supported living payment (permanent, severe restriction below 15 hours a week, or total blindness, at 16 or over; or full-time care of someone who would need institutional care, at 18 or 20). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Main benefit`  @desc The benefit applied for
      a IS AN Applicant  @desc Birth date, citizenship or visa, residence, other benefits, dependent children and relationship
      j IS A `Jobseeker facts`  @desc The jobseeker facts
      s IS A `Sole parent facts`  @desc The sole parent facts
      l IS A `Supported living facts`  @desc The supported living payment facts
      r IS A `Rate facts`  @desc The base rate, income test and weekly income
      d IS A DATE  @desc The day in question
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to` b `, applicant` a `, jobseeker facts` j `, sole parent facts` s `, supported living facts` l `, rate facts` r `, on` d IF
        NOT `is barred by ss 18 or 19` a
    AND CONSIDER b
        WHEN `jobseeker support` THEN `is entitled to jobseeker support` a j r d
        WHEN `jobseeker support on the ground of health condition, injury, or disability` THEN `is entitled to jobseeker support` a j r d
        WHEN `sole parent support` THEN `is entitled to sole parent support` a s d
        WHEN `supported living payment for restricted work capacity or total blindness` THEN `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` a l d
        WHEN `supported living payment for caring for another person` THEN `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` a l d
